! vfl_store_cross_fetch.strap -- a look-ahead level that FETCHES the second
! word of an earlier level's word-crossing VFL store waits for that store.
!
! FOUND 2026-11-17 by the 7030 STRAP II TABMAN test (tests/
! check_strap2_7030_tabman.py, step 3b). The sequence was TBEN3's
! "ST(BU,13),.1($4)" with $4 at bit 62 of a word, followed by
! "ST(BU,6),.14($4)" into the next word. The vle's 6-bit length field
! (46, bits 6-11 of the second word) came back 0. The per-operation VFL
! E-box times (StretchTiming.bsv) kept the crossing store pending while the
! second ST's level was loaded. That level fetched the second word, which
! the crossing store had not yet written, merged its field into it, and
! stored the stale word back.
!
! THE FIX (StretchIBox's levelStores): a level whose stored field crosses
! a word boundary stores storeAddr AND storeAddr + 1. The store-close-to-
! fetch wait (rl_prepare) and levelHolds now compare both words. Basis:
! Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-18, "VFL data with word boundary
! crossover represent inefficient use of LA levels". On the machine a
! crossing field takes a look-ahead level per word, each with its own
! store address. One level comparing two words is this model's CHOSEN
! stand-in; what the second level costs is not modelled.
!
! CASE 1, the hazard: LTRS(BU,64,8), 60 clocks in the E-box (PDF 123),
! keeps the four levels behind it pending. LI then ST(BU,13) at W0+.62
! puts 13 one-bits in W0 bits 62-63 and W1 bits 0-10. LI then
! ST(BU,6) at W1+.12 puts 6 in W1 bits 12-17.
!   W0 = (16)0000000000000003
!   W1 = (16)FFE1800000000000   (stale: (16)0001800000000000)
! CASE 2, the control: the same two stores into W2/W3 with an
! unconditional branch between them. The branch drains the look-ahead
! (StretchIBox's iboxHazard), so the hazard cannot arise and the values
! hold with or without the fix.
!   W2 = (16)0000000000000003, W3 = (16)FFE1800000000000
! Values hand-derived from the field positions (RefMan printed pp.21, 58).
!
! INJECTION, measured 2026-11-17: levelStores without the storeCross
! term. FAIL W1 = 0x0001800000000000 (the TABMAN symptom), and nothing
! else: W0, W2, W3 and the PC pass. The cycle count is in the run line.
!
        SLC, 1000.0
START   LTRS(BU,64,8), SLOW
        LI(BU,13), 8191
        ST(BU,13), W0+.62
        LI(BU,6), 6
        ST(BU,6), W1+.12
        LI(BU,13), 8191
        ST(BU,13), W2+.62
        B, NEXT
NEXT    LI(BU,6), 6
        ST(BU,6), W3+.12
DONE    BEW, $
        SLC, 1100.0
SLOW    DD(BU,64), 0
W0      DD(BU,64), 0
W1      DD(BU,64), 0
W2      DD(BU,64), 0
W3      DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
